        id: 'coral-belt', term: 'Coral belt and red belt',
        def: 'The belts above black. In the IBJJF system, the red and black belt represents the seventh degree and the red and white belt the eighth degree; both are commonly called coral belts. The red belt represents the ninth degree. The tenth degree was given only to the pioneers of Brazilian jiu-jitsu.',
