        def: 'In USA Judo, points earned by winning contests, which reduce the time in grade needed for the next dan rank. A win against an opponent of the same rank is credited as 1.0 point. For shodan, the time in grade falls from 3 years for a non-competitor to 6 months for a competitor with 20 points.',
        src: [3],
      },
      {
        id: 'rank-certificate', term: 'Rank certificate',
        def: 'The document that proves a rank. Some are issued by the school and some by a national or world body. The All United States Kendo Federation calls its certificate a menjo and tells members to keep it "as it is your proof of rank". Kukkiwon issues poom and dan certificates, and says only holders of Kukkiwon-certified ranks are eligible for international competitions run by World Taekwondo.',
        src: [5, 11],
      },
      {
        id: 'testing-cycle', term: 'Testing cycle',
        def: 'How often a school holds belt tests, for example every three months. Common usage; no body defines it.',
        src: [],
      },
