  <FeaturedAnswer question="What do kyu and dan mean?">
    Kyu and dan are the two sets of ranks used in Japanese martial arts. Kyu ranks are the student ranks below black belt and count down, so 1st kyu is the last rank before black belt. Dan ranks are the black belt ranks and count up from 1st dan. Taekwondo uses geup for color belts and dan, or poom under age 15, for black belts.
  </FeaturedAnswer>

  <section class="section bg-white pt-0">
